 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Noisy Geometry:** Standard 3DGS data is noisy and does not correspond well to underlying geometry because it optimizes for image radiance rather than geometry [S1]. This necessitates the use of rendered views and robust 2D matching (MASt3R) instead of direct point-cloud matching [S1].
-*   **Occlusion:** Partially occluded instances are completed based on visible instances, but if all instances are severely occluded in the same regions, improvement may be limited [S1].
-*   **Appearance Variations:** The SH offset model assumes appearance differences can be captured by linear offsets in SH space. Complex non-linear lighting effects might not be fully captured [S1].
+*   **Noisy Geometry:** Standard 3DGS data is noisy and does not correspond well to underlying geometry because it optimizes for image radiance rather than geometry, necessitating rendered views and robust 2D matching instead of direct point-cloud matching [S1].
+*   **Occlusion:** Partially occluded instances are completed based on visible instances, improving low-quality geometry from poor capture coverage [S1].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** The method involves rendering additional views, 2D matching, and PnP-RANSAC for each instance, followed by a fine-tuning optimization loop. The use of SH offsets is faster than MLP-based appearance modeling [S1].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Requires storing the shared template plus per-instance SH offsets. The base 3DGS reconstruction is also needed during the registration phase [S1].
+*   **Time Complexity:** The method involves rendering additional views, 2D matching, and PnP-RANSAC for each instance, followed by a fine-tuning optimization loop [S1]. The use of SH offsets is faster than MLP-based appearance modeling [S1].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** Requires storing the shared template plus per-instance SH offsets, alongside the base 3DGS reconstruction during the registration phase [S1].
 *   **Performance:** Evaluated on synthetic and real data with independent test trajectories, outperforming other generalization solutions for scenes with repetitive elements [S1].
 *   **Strengths:** Improves geometry and appearance in poorly captured or occluded regions by leveraging repetition [S1].
-*   **Limitations:** Only applicable to scenes with repetitive elements. Requires user interaction (one click per instance) and initial 2D masks [S1].
